            <ArticleTitle>Excision of right coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2010.01130.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A coronary artery aneurysm (CAA), the etiology and treatment of which are still not fully understood, is uncommonly encountered. A giant CAA is extremely rare and only a limited number of cases have been reported. We report the case of a 37-year-old female with a giant right coronary artery aneurysm that was successfully treated by surgical excision.</AbstractText>
